From 8bf3b2ac6492621d4441fef70bfcee784184352d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DH2Work <dh2work@localhost>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 00:42:35 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] DH2Work: T32 ARMv8 acquire/release + CRC32, and arm64 A32
 halt guard

Two independent changes needed by the DH2Work A32 host at pin 86458a0b.

1. backend/arm64/a32_address_space.cpp: do not run A32GetSetElimination when
   check_halt_on_memory_access is set. A halting memory access can end a block
   before that pass has committed guest register writes, which would report
   stale registers to the callbacks. The A64 arm64 backend and both x64
   backends already carry this guard.

2. frontend/A32: add the Thumb-2 encodings and translator bodies for the
   ARMv8-A acquire/release and exclusive acquire/release accesses (LDAB, LDAH,
   LDAEX, LDAEXB, LDAEXH, LDAEXD, STLB, STLH, STLEX, STLEXB, STLEXH, STLEXD)
   and for CRC32/CRC32C in byte, halfword and word sizes. The ARM-state
   frontend already implements all of these; the T32 decoder had only STL and
   LDA. The AOSP ARM32 sysroot reaches them on the dynamic linker and scudo
   mutex/allocator paths.

Re-derived from the ARM ARM and the in-tree A32 implementations.
---
 src/dynarmic/CMakeLists.txt                   |   1 +
 .../backend/arm64/a32_address_space.cpp       |   6 +-
 src/dynarmic/frontend/A32/decoder/thumb32.inc |  20 +++
 .../A32/translate/impl/a32_translate_impl.h   |  14 ++
 .../A32/translate/impl/thumb32_crc32.cpp      |  77 ++++++++++
 .../impl/thumb32_load_store_dual.cpp          | 144 ++++++++++++++++++
 6 files changed, 261 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 src/dynarmic/frontend/A32/translate/impl/thumb32_crc32.cpp

